{"title":"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three congruent isosceles triangles are constructed with their bases on the sides of an equilateral triangle of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  The sum of the areas of the three isosceles triangles is the same as the area of the equilateral triangle.  What is the length of one of the two congruent sides of one of the isosceles triangles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c0c50bd24a380ae01c4141c2e203ee7d5bde350.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}4\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}3\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\dfrac23\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}2\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"432\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Reflect each of the triangles over its respective side.  Then since the areas of the triangles total to the area of the equilateral triangle, it can be seen that the triangles fill up the equilateral one and the vertices of these triangles concur at the circumcenter of the equilateral triangle.  Hence the desired answer is just its circumradius, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ea1170c77a4f71712472a0e0bc30dd7129c661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}3\\textbf{ (B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"76\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>(Solution by djmathman)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the total area of each <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruent_(geometry)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Congruent (geometry)\">congruent</a> isosceles triangle is the same, the area of each is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69e75241b5dc755a5b395b748fc53018d642bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> the total <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area_of_an_equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Area of an equilateral triangle\">area of the equilateral triangle</a> of side length 1, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69e75241b5dc755a5b395b748fc53018d642bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> x <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b30d1822446a0286407f9070fe08a4eaeeb1ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />. Likewise, the area of each can be defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c95a1e861eb151fdc2fa3cf0ee4cff81928b47e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{bh}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> equaling 1, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a9023308e90d7a0d8333ba1f335d1bf32bc5941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{h}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"37\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69e75241b5dc755a5b395b748fc53018d642bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> x <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b30d1822446a0286407f9070fe08a4eaeeb1ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/47666f5e057ca830d70a60689ed42744e1cd7880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />. A side length of the isosceles triangle is the hypotenuse with legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/61973d2d272346b3842846d75d26d27dddc40c0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{b}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Using the Pythagorean Theorem, the side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4fcb6d69e20ef6630d888094d9d0989fde27a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{{(\\dfrac{1}2)}^2 + {(\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}6)}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ea1170c77a4f71712472a0e0bc30dd7129c661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}3\\textbf{ (B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"76\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>(Solution by johnstucky)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that each of the congruent sides meets at the circumcenter of the equilateral triangle. Therefore, they are equal to the circumradius. The area is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b4eb0cb5269e1069fdc002af68949a73de272f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0c7d6e8449f1fba08fd4784ac989dfe40f3679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />. The area can also be found using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de697c8744e7a95426a25f87a9beecda5c47d4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{4}s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"41\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53837f2ded54e102c94834d7ea63a3ea8a619798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />. Setting these equal and solving entails <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5fce5cba2815083ea93a0985e0d8e255bfc268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"30\" height=\"43\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ea1170c77a4f71712472a0e0bc30dd7129c661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}3\\textbf{ (B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"76\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>solution by Proper\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\nAdditional Insight:\nAfter noting that the congruent sides meet at the circumcenter, you can just use the Extended Law of Sines to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e8718f0ab5ea314cd7933a766d7157c80d48501b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sin 60^{\\circ}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"43\" />, which is choice B\n~Extremelysupercooldude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5jwD5UViZO8?t=1013\">https://youtu.be/5jwD5UViZO8?t=1013</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rJytKoJzNBY\">https://youtu.be/rJytKoJzNBY</a>\n</p><p>solution by sugar_rush\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A\">2014 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233715\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 234/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2296/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4835/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.324      1 -total\n 57.19%    7.620      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 40.46%    5.391      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12353:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233715 and revision id 187310. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}